def fix_mc(w):
    # w is already lowercased base form, e.g. "mcdonald"
    if w.startswith("mc") and len(w) > 2:
        return "Mc" + w[2:].capitalize()
    return w.capitalize()

The key is applying exactly one transform per token and appending once — so don't both capitalize() AND add a Mc-variant.

